WEBVTT

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.670
I was once just like you.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:24.170
Whatever do you mean?

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:28.300
Long ago, I never believed in miracles.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.720
No matter how many
worlds we lived through,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.890
or how many blessings came upon us,

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:39.020
I realized there was nothing
we could do to change our prescribed fate.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.980
I expected nothing from the world!

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.770
Because expectations
lead to disappointment!

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:50.450
I never believed in miracles,
because they would never happen!

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.860
But still, I learned!

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:58.700
From Keiichi, from Rena, from Mion,
from Shion, and from Satoko, too!

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.460
Miracles don't happen on their own--
you have to <i>make </i>them happen!

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.890
I tire of this.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:27.070
I tire of this charade.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.920
You are so terribly boring.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.150
Do it.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:16.570
Erase me from your world.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:23.200
You'll make much fancier friends
at St. Lucia Academy.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.130
That doesn't sound bad.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:32.340
But you'll realize something
after you kill me.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.550
You'll know you were
happiest here in Hinamizawa.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:41.810
That I was the one who cared
about you more than anyone!

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.360
I already know that! You think I didn't?!

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:58.410
I <i>know </i>you care about me more than anyone!

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:03.250
I care about <i>you </i>more than anyone!

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:06.830
It's been that way for <i>years</i>!

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:11.130
How the hell would I not know that?!

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:16.130
You want me to erase you from my world?

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:20.680
I'll never do that! I never <i>could</i>!

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.220
So I'll punch you instead!
As hard as I can!

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.230
Until your face swells up!

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:29.770
I'll beat those math drills
into your head...

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.570
...until you can solve every last problem!

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.200
No, no, no, no, no!

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.950
I don't want to!

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:40.820
I don't want to study!

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.780
I hate it, I hate it, I <i>hate it</i>!

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.370
I don't even want to
<i>think </i>about it, or <i>look </i>at it!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:49.000
I just want to play and have fun!

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.790
I just want to be with you, Rika!

00:03:56.630 --> 00:04:01.260
You little brat! Stop being
so goddamn selfish already!

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:06.140
What?! Says you! Stop forcing me
to go along with <i>your </i>dream!

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.480
You're so stupid, Satoko!

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.310
You don't know anything, Rika!

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:06.370
Hmm? What are you doing?

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:09.410
A miracle will never side with you.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.250
I asked what you are doing.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:20.260
If we fall into the pit of despair
a hundred times,

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:22.380
then we climb up two hundred times.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:25.260
If we're pulled into the whirlpool
of tragedy a thousand times,

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:28.100
then we fight back two thousand times!

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:36.730
Because a miracle
will <i>always </i>side with us!

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:51.910
Rika and I are going to destroy our fate!

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:55.000
We're going to make our miracle happen!

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.590
Do you know how many endless days
have brought us to this moment?!

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.820
Rika and I...

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:27.200
...and Keiichi, and Rena...

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.950
...and Mion, and Shion...

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.460
...and <i>everyone </i>in Hinamizawa...

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.130
...even Satoko...

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:41.210
...are stronger than you think!

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:50.310
How very interesting, my darling failure!

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:53.430
You deserve a reward
for such fine performance!

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:08.660
Strike true, Onigari-no-Ryuuou!

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:12.240
Devour her sins, one and all!

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:33.640
Impudent worm!

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:36.890
You swore to me that
if I showed you a miracle,

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:39.150
you would leave this world,

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.770
forever!

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:43.940
Very well.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:49.820
Failure as you are, you <i>did</i>
miraculously strike back at me...

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.970
You should follow <i>my </i>dream instead, Rika!

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:16.140
Live here in Hinamizawa with me forever!

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:21.440
No, I'm not giving up on my dream!
You're coming with me to St. Lucia!

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:24.570
Well, I'm not giving up on mine, either!

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:27.110
I'm living with you in Hinamizawa!

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:30.450
Satoko! I just want
to be with you forever!

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:34.200
Rika! I just want to be with you forever!

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:38.160
I want to go to St. Lucia with you!

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.330
I don't want to go!
I don't want to let you go!

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.540
Satoko!

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.760
Rika!

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.370
Hey, Satoko?

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.080
Yes?

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.670
I'm sorry for leaving you
all on your lonesome.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:31.130
From here on out, I'll keep
my eyes on you. I'll help you study.

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:34.840
Thank you, Rika.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.060
I've lost count of the years,

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:43.100
but it seems they were
worth it in the end.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:49.730
I'm sorry. I'm too stupid.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:55.530
No matter how hard you try to make me,
I'll never study that hard again.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:57.160
I figured.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:01.080
How many years did I
make you study for that exam?

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.370
I can't remember.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:05.790
Think of the biggest number you can,

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:09.500
then multiply it by three.
That's how many.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:13.510
It's easy for looping lives
to develop "allergies."

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:18.510
In the end, just looking at the problem
makes you break out in hives.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.640
I thought if I kept studying,

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:24.440
then I'd get to stay
with you in the same class.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:29.520
That was the whole reason
I worked so hard for so long.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:33.530
If you gave it that much effort,
and still had terrible grades,

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:36.740
then maybe you really
<i>aren't </i>cut out for schoolwork.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:40.490
It took you this long to realize that?

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:55.760
Hey, there they are!

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:00.510
Keiichi-<i>kun</i>! We found them!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.350
They're over here!

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:04.520
What the heck are they doing over here?

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:10.860
Whoa, Rika-<i>chan</i>?! And you too, Satoko!
What happened to your clothes?!

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:13.490
Whoa, your faces are all beat up!

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:17.950
Oh, yikes! I think we might have
bandages in the car!

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:24.080
I'm fine. Rika's weak punches barely hurt.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:28.120
Though I'm pretty sure
they <i>did </i>make you cry.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:31.290
My, you should see your own eyes, Rika.
They're so very red.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.550
Okay, that's enough!

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:37.680
What the heck made you guys
break into a full-on fist fight?

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:56.530
I'm glad we came to get you guys.

00:11:56.530 --> 00:12:01.120
So, what were you fighting about?
Let this old fart help.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:07.210
C'mon, you can tell me!
Aren't we friends?!

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:12.210
Mii-<i>chan</i>, I'm sure
they've already talked it over.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:15.630
So the reason they started fighting
isn't important anymore.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:19.550
You're too good at this, Rena.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.310
You guys okay?

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:24.850
I wouldn't say okay.

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:27.430
I'd say our friendship
has thoroughly ended.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:29.770
That's what I was going to say.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:32.020
You know something?

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:36.280
No one has to do everything together
until the end--not even twins.

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:41.450
Even if they'll never forget
the wonderful time they spent together...

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:47.700
...they don't <i>have</i>
to always stay together.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:51.960
Even twins can grow apart. Family, too.

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:56.000
That doesn't mean
your relationship is over.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:01.130
Can I add something to that,
Satoko, Rika-<i>chan</i>?

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:05.350
You know what I think a friend is?

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:10.020
Even if you're not with someone,
or don't want to see someone again,

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:12.230
when you see them down the line,

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:20.240
you both know you'll always have
that relationship with them.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:25.700
That's what it means
to be friends with someone.

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:29.450
The word "friendship"
doesn't shackle you to someone.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:33.630
If you think you always have to be
with someone to be their friend,

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:36.130
then I think you've got
the wrong idea about friendship.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:17.370
"Hinamizawa"

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:23.010
Morning, Keiichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:25.050
Why are you always here so early?

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:29.600
You can sleep in every now and then...
actually, maybe not.

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:32.060
I totally can't! Not today!

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:37.940
Morning, guys! Glad you're not late!

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:42.030
We couldn't be late! If we missed out
on today's big event, I'd be so upset!

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:45.910
Yeah! After all, today's the day
when our dear friend

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.660
sets off on her big adventure!

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:24.610
"Sunday, March 29th"

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:41.080
Shinkansen Track 16

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:48.010
Give it everything you've got, Rika-<i>chan</i>.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:51.850
And don't forget that
Hinamizawa school club spirit!

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:54.430
You can do anything you set
your mind to, I know it, Rika-<i>chan</i>!

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:57.230
You've got endorsements from the first
and second club presidents, after all!

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:58.440
Mm-hmm!

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:05.360
You look <i>so kyute </i>in your
St. Lucia uniform! I wanna take you home!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.610
But then I couldn't take the train.

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:17.000
Thank you for riding the Shinkansen.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:23.880
The 12:52 Hikari for Tokyo
is arriving on track number 15.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:26.670
Please stand behind the yellow line.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:36.270
Right, well, I'm off.

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:43.570
How are you <i>just </i>getting here, Satoko?!

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:48.400
She'll be back in three years.
If she doesn't get held back, of course!

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:55.370
Wait, hold on! I haven't passed on
Shion's message yet!

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:56.370
C'mon.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:57.700
Let them talk!

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:00.670
--All right, let's go, Mion.
--Let's go, Mii-<i>chan</i>!

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:02.630
So this is goodbye.

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:05.750
Do enjoy life all on your lonesome.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:11.590
Unfortunately, I recall you telling me
I'll make many lovely friends there.

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:17.140
You will. So many fancy friends
who will be perfectly suited for you.

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:21.100
Still, you won't be there, Satoko.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:24.770
True. And you won't be here, Rika.

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:31.030
We're the only looping lives
in this entire universe.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:38.120
And because our lives are eternal,
sometimes we need to be apart.

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:40.710
So we don't grow sick of one another.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:43.920
To strengthen our bonds of friendship.

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:50.170
But if I don't see you for a while,
I'll come looking for you.

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.930
If you come after me, I'll run away.

00:17:52.930 --> 00:17:55.760
If you stop coming after me,
you'll find me.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:58.810
If you go north, I'll go south.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:01.890
If you go east, I'll go west.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:03.190
We'll see each other again someday.

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:05.230
Sooner than we think.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.780
When they cry--whoever <i>they </i>are.

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:52.530
Oh?

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:06.000
Have a good year, everyone!

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:43.740
Gogura Airport

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:03.090
Irie Clinic

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:10.400
You came back!

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:37.470
Where am I...?

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:38.840
Where's Satoko?

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:57.780
Hey, Satoko!

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:10.370
Check this out! I got this
awesome meat at a super low price!

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:11.710
Why so much?

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:16.840
Well, I also got a bunch of veggies
that were on sale,

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:20.300
so I figured we could have ourselves
a <i>sukiyaki </i>party tonight!

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:23.850
I'm not quite in the mood for a party.

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:26.810
Heyo! It's your Nee-Nee!

00:21:26.810 --> 00:21:28.520
Whoa, Shion-<i>san</i>!

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:32.060
I wish I could've seen
little miss Rika off!

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:35.610
I can't believe Uncle Yoshiro
made me work!

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:37.730
Hey there, Uncle Teppei!

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:41.280
Goodness, you're not going to eat
all that by yourselves, are you?

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:45.120
You're more than welcome to join us!

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:49.450
This simply isn't for me.

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:52.540
It's about time for me
to come after you, Rika.

00:22:03.720 --> 00:22:06.600
Very well, Satoko Hojo.

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:08.890
I'll return yourself to you.

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:20.740
What's up?

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:23.530
Are you feeling okay?

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:32.040
I'm right as rain!

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:35.130
A <i>sukiyaki </i>party sounds lovely!

00:22:35.130 --> 00:22:39.630
Watch out, or I'll steal all the yummy
bits out from underneath you!

00:22:39.630 --> 00:22:44.260
Sure, but I bought enough
to counter that plan of yours!

00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:47.640
My, you're quite good at this too, Uncle!

00:22:49.310 --> 00:22:54.440
You've trained me well, Satoko!
I'm a supermarket shopper extraordinaire!

00:22:54.440 --> 00:22:59.360
This is still so much food. Why don't we
invite Kei-<i>chan </i>and Rena-<i>san</i>, too?

00:22:59.360 --> 00:23:02.690
Oh, I can call my sister, too!

00:23:04.030 --> 00:23:06.240
Well, speak of the devil...

00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:14.370
Keiichi-<i>san</i>! Rena-<i>san</i>! Mion-<i>san</i>!
